<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-12">
  <header class="text-center mb-16">
    <h1 class="text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-tighter italic mb-4">Project <span class="text-primary">Genesis</span></h1>
    <p class="text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-slate-500">The History of WWWorkRemote</p>
  </header>

  <div class="space-y-12">
    <section class="card-neural p-10">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-blue-400 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-blue-400"></span> 01_THE_VISION
      </h2>
      <div class="prose-invert text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        <p class="mb-4">WWWorkRemote was born out of a necessity to cut through the noise of the global remote job market. What started as a simple scraper has evolved into a sophisticated <strong>Autonomous Synthesis Engine</strong> designed to ingest, normalize, and intelligently categorize job postings from the far corners of the digital workspace.</p>
        <p>The goal is simple: total informational parity. By consolidating disparate signals into a high-density, vector-indexed repository, we empower developers to find their next mission without the friction of traditional job boards.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card-neural p-10 border-l-4 border-l-primary">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-primary"></span> 02_NEURAL_EVOLUTION
      </h2>
      <div class="prose-invert text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        <p class="mb-4">In 2026, the project underwent a radical transformation. Moving away from standard cloud-dependent APIs, we embraced a <strong>Local-First LLM Architecture</strong>. Utilizing the power of Qwen 2.5 Coder and llama.cpp, WWWorkRemote now performs complex classification, sentiment analysis, and tech-stack extraction on-premise.</p>
        <p>This shift not only ensures data privacy and operational independence but also allows for high-concurrency processing via a modern Fiber-based Async architecture.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card-neural p-10 border-t border-white/5 bg-gradient-to-br from-base-200 to-base-300">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-emerald-400 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span> 03_THE_STACK
      </h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 font-mono text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-500">
        <div class="p-4 bg-white/5 rounded border border-white/5">
          <div class="mb-1 text-slate-600">Core_Node</div>
          <div class="text-white">Rails 8</div>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-white/5 rounded border border-white/5">
          <div class="mb-1 text-slate-600">Neural_Link</div>
          <div class="text-white">RubyLLM</div>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-white/5 rounded border border-white/5">
          <div class="mb-1 text-slate-600">Vector_Store</div>
          <div class="text-white">PgVector</div>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-white/5 rounded border border-white/5">
          <div class="mb-1 text-slate-600">Interface</div>
          <div class="text-white">Dracula Pro</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="text-center pt-8">
      <%= link_to root_path, class: "text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 hover:text-white transition-colors" do %>
        &larr; Return to Central Command
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
